ChooChooTracker on Mortar (MORTAR_BUILD, on top of the Linux desktop build).
Every change is behind MORTAR_BUILD; other builds are unchanged.

- corelib_file.cpp: the install is read-only (Nix store), so always use the
  per-user data directory the AppImage build uses
  ($XDG_DATA_HOME/ChooChooTracker); the launcher seeds it.
- corelib_gfx.cpp: open fullscreen at the panel's native size and pick the
  largest built-in font that fits (1024x768 -> 24x36 cells, a 960x720
  grid, centred), as the handheld builds do, instead of the desktop's
  fixed 640x480 canvas scaled by 1.6.
- corelib_input.cpp: default gamepad EDIT/OPT by the Brick's labels
  (A = BTN_EAST = SDL "B", B = BTN_SOUTH = SDL "A"), and show the labels
  on the key-mapping screen.
- corelib_mainloop.cpp: the handhelds' idle frame-rate throttle.
- common.cpp: default audio 44.1 kHz (the codec's dmix rate, no
  resampling) and the handhelds' 512-frame buffer.

